      "image": null,
      "content": "Data pipelines that glue preprocessing libraries to deep learning frameworks frequently break at runtime. A mismatched schema or an unhandled null value usually escapes detection until execution hits an expensive training epoch or GPU batch.\n\nXazz solves this boundary problem by implementing a custom domain-specific language in Rust. It unifies Polars preprocessing and Burn deep learning compilation into a single statically checked workflow. Data transformations gain compile-time null and type safety before anything executes.\n\nThe real architectural win is zero-copy data transfer. Intermediate states transition directly from Apache Arrow structures into Burn tensors without serialization overhead. It pairs static verification with SHA-256 audit logs to enforce deterministic execution across environments.\n\nPushing data pipeline validation into the compilation phase removes an entire class of runtime infrastructure bugs."
